  "name": "Qwen 3.8 Flash Next (180B-A6B, 4-bit)",
  "description": "Qwen's experimental preview of the architecture behind Qwen4: a 125B-parameter MoE with 6B active per token, plus a 51B n-gram embedding table. Gezel offers the 94 GB Unsloth UD-IQ4_XS split GGUF for llama.cpp and the verified 112 GB native MLX Community group-32 conversion for Apple silicon. With mlx-vlm 0.7.1, Gezel memory-maps the MLX build's 29.80 GiB PLE table instead of wiring it into Metal; the measured fixed working set is about 75.2 GiB after the first live batch, and a 128 GB Mac is recommended.",
